      "version": "2.0.0",
      "description": "<p>Finally managed to render the range readout actually in the scope without causing all sorts of glitches 🥳</p>\n<p>All other render modes were removed and the mod slimmed down, only a simple fallback for PiP-Disabler remains.</p>\n<h2>Important Note</h2>\n<p>If you already have custom per-scope offset presets defined, those will be deleted on first start.<br />\nThat is necessary because they would no longer align with the new coordinate system.<br />\nVanilla presets are now shipped and stored seperatly to your own.</p>\n<p>See full <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://github.com/maschine34675/ScopeRangefinder/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">CHANGELOG.md</a></p>\n",
